      "id": "hackernews-2026-08-13-show-hn-ballet-workflow-automation-that-writes-integrations-",
      "title": "Show HN: Ballet – Workflow automation that writes integrations against any API",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.ballet.dev/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49280184\nPoints: 29\n# Comments: 7",
      "body": "Your most ambitious automations shouldn’t stay in your backlog Get started    Built by the team behind Brainfish, trusted by:     How it worksSkip the engineering queue. Ballet automates your team’s best ideas across your revenue stack. Growth ideas stall when they need systems connected, and engineering roadmaps aren’t fast enough. Ballet is the fix. Describe the outcome — lead routing, attribution, a renewal play — and Ballet builds it, runs it, keeps it working.      Use casesWhen automations build themselves, your team is more focused.    Marketing Instant lead capture to CRM Enrich, dedupe, and score every inbound lead against your own product usage before it routes, no overnight batch job and no data-eng request.     Framer    Your products DB    Salesforce    BigQuery    Revenue Ops Account surge detection Spot meaningful changes in your product telemetry, enrich them, and push a next-best-action to the right rep so sales acts on real signals, not stale CRM fields.     Your telemetry DB    Clay    ZoomInfo    Salesforce    Slack    Sales Ops Order changes (without ENG ticket) Let ops or AEs amend pricing, terms, or SKUs and propagate it through your internal billing, not just the CRM.     Salesforce CPQ    Stripe    Your Billing service    Freshdesk         IntegrationsConnect to the systems your workflows already depend on     How we compareBuilt for the integrations your stack hasn’t considered       AI Agents (e.g. Claude)Traditional workflow tools (e.g. n8n)   Speed to build Minutes, plain English Fast to start Weeks, by hand  Connects to internal systems Reaches your proprietary systems Limited Not without weeks of ENG effort  Consistency Same output every time Different & unpredictable Consistent but rigid  Reasoning Flexible and considered Deep reasoning Inflexible, can't adapt  Auditable Yes, transparent code Minimal reporting Minimal reporting  Cost Predictable Expensive Climbs with volume       Ballet is a workflow-automation platform from the team behind Brainfish. Describe a multi-system outcome in plain English and Ballet builds it as reviewable, version-controlled code — deterministic where accuracy matters, agentic where judgment helps.  Connector libraries cap out when your stack is proprietary or the graph gets huge. Ballet writes the integration against any API the moment you need it, and the workflow runs as inspectable code instead of a brittle visual graph.  Yes where it matters. Ballet writes deterministic workflow code your engineers can read, approve, and replay. Agentic reasoning is used only on steps that benefit from flexibility — not on the steps that must never drift.  Design partners with real multi-system workflows stuck behind an engineering queue — RevOps, Support Ops, and product-led growth teams. You bring one backlog workflow; we model it on your systems in a short working session.  Generated code is visible and version-controlled, with approval gates and replayable runs. Ballet is part of Brainfish and covered by Brainfish’s SOC2 Type II compliance. Details live in the Trust Center at https://trust.brainfi.sh/.  Brainfish is the knowledge layer; Ballet is the execution layer. Customers can trigger Ballet workflows from Brainfish, and Ballet also runs standalone against your existing stack.     Let’s goBring the workflow that’s been in your backlog for two quarters. We’ll model it in Ballet on your real systems in a 30-minute working session. No SOW, no scope creep. One of our specialists runs it with you. Get started",
