    {
      "id": "hackernews-2026-08-12-thanks-to-social-media-canned-sardines-are-a-scarcity-on-the",
      "title": "Thanks to social media, canned sardines are a scarcity on the supermarket shelf",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://corneroffifth.studio/why-cant-you-find-canned-sardines-right-now/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49279013\nPoints: 145\n# Comments: 188",
      "body": "Thanks to social media, canned sardines are a scarcity on the supermarket shelf. If you’ve noticed empty shelves where canned sardines used to sit at your local grocery store, you aren’t imagining things. Supermarkets across the country are facing a noticeable shortage of the popular staple, leaving shoppers scrambling to find their favorite brands. The missing tins are the resultThanks to social media, canned sardines are a scarcity on the supermarket shelf.If you’ve noticed empty shelves where canned sardines used to sit at your local grocery store, you aren’t imagining things. Supermarkets across the country are facing a noticeable shortage of the popular staple, leaving shoppers scrambling to find their favorite brands. The missing tins are the result of a sudden spike in popularity colliding with severe environmental problems out at sea.For generations, canned sardines were seen as a cheap, humble pantry item. That changed recently as social media trends and a growing interest in high-protein, healthy foods turned tinned seafood into a viral food craze.What is the Viral Sardine Diet Trend?One of the top social media trends touts a sardine-only diet that lasts one to three days. The short-term viral fad diet involves eating the tinned fish while drinking only water, black coffee or plain tea. The result of a protein-only, zero carbs diet is significant weight loss. The trend took off across TikTok, YouTube and health/keto communities — promoted by figures like Dr. Annette Bosworth (Dr. Boz) and Dr. Mindy Pelz. The trend is also immensely popular with the fashion world as it is seen as a low-cost alternative to Ozempic.However, as millions of new buyers began seeking out omega-3 rich snacks, demand soared practically overnight. But there’s a bigger problem at hand.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "carabiner",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-12T21:45:29.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://corneroffifth.studio/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Fish_Graphics3.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://corneroffifth.studio/why-cant-you-find-canned-sardines-right-now/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-08-12-fernandes-the-centre-of-attention-but-what-next-for-man-utd-",
      "title": "Fernandes the centre of attention - but what next for Man Utd captain?",
      "summary": "Manchester United skipper Bruno Fernandes is attracting attention on and off the pitch.",
      "body": "Bruno Fernandes was the centre of attention in every sense on a historic night at Croke Park.One of the biggest cheers of the evening from a sell-out crowd for the first 'soccer' match between English teams at the 82,500-capacity home of the Gaelic Athletic Association came after an hour of Manchester United's pre-season game with Leeds, when Fernandes' name was read out as one of five substitutes being made by head coach Michael Carrick.The place would have erupted if either Fernandes had not had an effort ruled out for offside, or his shot from the edge of the area had gone in, not flicked off the bar.The hero worship was taken too far when first one fan, then another, then another raced on to the pitch to get a selfie. With chaos threatening to take hold and 90 minutes played, the match was called to a halt without injury time, and went straight to penalties.Amazingly, Fernandes missed, although Noussair Mazraoui kept his cool a few minutes later to secure a 5-4 victory, after the game itself had been brought to a premature conclusion at 1-1.The result was irrelevant compared to preparations for the new season.But the reaction for Fernandes underlines his hero status among United fans, which  was established long before his nine goals and record 21 assists ensured a third-place finish in the Premier League last season and secured a return to the Champions League.Of all United's squad, Fernandes is the one worshipped by fans.But after the 'will-he, won't-he' debate around the 31-year-old's future last summer when the massive offer from Saudi Pro-League side Al-Hilal emerged, United's resolve could be about to be tested again.Italian heavyweights Juventus and AC Milan, plus Galatasaray, are all understood to be keen on the Portugal playmaker, who has a £57m release clause available to overseas clubs.It remains to be seen how United react if a bid is received. Last December, Fernandes admitted to being \"hurt\" at being told by United officials it was up to him whether he wanted to accept the Al-Hilal offer.Now, his contract has entered its final year - there is an option to extend by a further season - and, as yet, there is no agreement over a new one.It is thought Fernandes' preference is to stay at United, potentially for the remainder of his career. On the club's previous visit to the Republic of Ireland in April, he said he wants to compete for trophies. That situation is understood still to be the case.But at a time when United are attempting to keep a lid on their wage bill, Fernandes could justifiably point to his contribution as being worthy of a significant salary, as Marcus Rashford returns to the club and is currently the highest earner.United's hierarchy may find themselves with a problem that won't easily be resolved.Certainly, Carrick won't want to lose the former Sporting man.Already, Fernandes' partnership with new arrival Youri Tielemans is starting to pay dividends.It was Tielemans who set his captain up for the shot that struck the bar, the short pass evidence of the understanding developing between the pair, which the Belgium midfielder outlined speaking to the media on Tuesday.Marcus Rashford, along with England team-mate Kobbie Mainoo and Argentina defender Lisandro Martinez, were not involved in the game.Rashford and Mainoo returned to training on Monday after their World Cup stints, with Martinez arriving in Dublin a day later after reaching the final.They could come into contention for Saturday's final pre-season game against AC Milan in Wroclaw.For Rashford, it would mean an encounter with Ruben Amorim, who he fell out with within weeks of his arrival from Sporting in November 2024. Amorim famously did not pick Mainoo to start a Premier League game before he was sacked in January.It had not been anticipated Rashford would return to United when he joined Barcelona on loan just over 12 months ago.However, Barca opted not to pay the £26m needed to make the transfer permanent and now it looks increasingly likely Rashford will remain with United and play under Carrick, a former team-mate, coach and, for three games following Ole Gunnar Solskjaer's dismissal in November 2021, temporary boss.\"He's our player,\" Carrick told ITV. \"He's come back great.\"I've known him a long time and he gives us something a little bit different.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-12T21:40:45.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_sport/1200/cpsprodpb/0191/live/999f6a80-968e-11f1-870d-5d08c49babb2.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cvgwzegz9ggo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "readTimeMinutes": 4,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "theverge-2026-08-12-pixel-11-event-live-blog-let-8217-s-watch-trevor-noah-introd",
      "title": "Pixel 11 event live blog: Let&#8217;s watch Trevor Noah introduce Google&#8217;s new phones",
      "summary": "It's almost time for the Made by Google keynote, where the company will show off the brand-new Pixel hardware it announced today. Like last year, it'll be a celebrity-packed live show, though Trevor Noah is hosting instead of Jimmy Fallon. If the 2025 show was any indication, today's broadcast might be something of a cringefest.\nIf you've been following tech news this morning, you already know a l",
      "body": "It’s almost time for the Made by Google keynote, where the company will show off the brand-new Pixel hardware it announced today. Like last year, it’ll be a celebrity-packed live show, though Trevor Noah is hosting instead of Jimmy Fallon. If the 2025 show was any indication, today’s broadcast might be something of a cringefest.\nIf you’ve been following tech news this morning, you already know a lot about the new Pixels. Press and creators were able to publish extensive hands-on impressions of the new hardware hours ago, and you can read our coverage of the Pixel 11 phones, their new camera features, the Pixel Watch 5, and more right now.\nGoogle could pull something unexpected out of a hat. But it seems more likely that this show isn’t for the people who devour every hands-on the moment they’re published. Instead, the event is likely intended to reach a more mainstream audience that might watch the livestream after work or as a replay at a later time.\nVictoria Song will be there in person, while the rest of us will be watching remotely, and we’ll all be blogging all of our secondhand embarrassment right here.\nThings kick off at 6PM ET / 3PM PT. You can watch the event on the embedded YouTube video while following along with our live thoughts below.",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Gadgets",
        "Google",
        "Google Pixel",
        "Mobile",
        "News",
        "Phones",
        "Smartwatch",
        "Tech",
        "Wearable"
      ],
      "author": "Jay Peters",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-12T21:30:00.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/Google-Pixel-11-Hot-pink.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,10.731298651824,100,78.537402696352",
