      "id": "techcrunch-2026-08-11-openai-launches-chatgpt-desktop-app-for-linux",
      "title": "OpenAI launches ChatGPT desktop app for Linux",
      "summary": "OpenAI is finally bringing a dedicated ChatGPT desktop app to Linux operating systems.",
      "body": "12:15 PM PDT · August 11, 2026\nImage Credits:Olivier Morin/AFP / Getty Images\nChatGPT is on desktops across the world, but there’s been one place where it’s been lacking: the Linux community. Certain sectors of the open source developer community have been clamoring for OpenAI to bring its chatbot to their neck of the woods.\nAs of this week, OpenAI has rectified this oversight, launching a dedicated ChatGPT app for Linux.\n“Linux has been one of the most-requested platforms for the desktop app, and this launch extends ChatGPT and Codex across every major desktop operating system,” the company said Tuesday.\nThe new app, which is being released in preview, will give Linux users the ability to use ChatGPT, ChatGPT Work, and Codex on a number of different distributions. The release is worldwide, as of Tuesday.\nOpenAI says that the distros that will be supported include desktop variants of Ubuntu 24.04 and 26.04 LTS, Debian 13, and Fedora 43 and 44. The totality of the Linux community comprises hundreds of distributions, although the distros that OpenAI has chosen here act as the base for a variety of “downstream” desktop distros or “flavors,” which should also be compatible with OpenAI’s apps as a result.\nOpenAI is a little behind Anthropic, which released a Claude desktop app for Linux about a month ago. Anthropic’s app is available for Ubuntu 22.04 or later and Debian 12 or later.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
